cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "SGTA: a pre-registered study of hidden-state stability and confident LLM errors"
type: software
version: 0.7.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ellischment/sgta-research-preview"
url: "https://ellischment.ru"
authors:
  - family-names: Popova
    given-names: Vasilisa
    affiliation: "Central University"
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered study of whether the stability of an LLM's hidden state
  separates a confident error from a confident correct answer, in the regime
  where hidden-state geometry cannot. The protocol, thresholds and kill rules
  are frozen before data and checked by hash in CI. No results on real data yet.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - uncertainty quantification
  - confident errors
  - pre-registration
